  "body": "# Summary\n\nThe Accountant counts Portfolio Margin supplied balances from HyperCore precompile 0x811, but it does not subtract Portfolio Margin borrow debt. A Vault account can therefore owe USDC borrow debt while Monetrix still reports the supplied collateral as full backing.\n\nThis creates false surplus. The normal yield flow can bridge, settle, and distribute that false surplus as yield, leaving USDM undercollateralized by the ignored borrow.\n\n# Root Cause\n\nPrecompileReader.suppliedBalance() decodes the 0x811 response as four uint64 words and returns only the fourth word:\n\n```solidity\n(,,, supplied) = abi.decode(res, (uint64, uint64, uint64, uint64));\n```\n\nHyperCore's `0x811` state contains both borrow and supply values. Monetrix adds the supply side into `_readL1Backing()` but never subtracts `borrow.value`.\n\n```solidity\nstruct BasisAndValue {\n    uint64 basis;\n    uint64 value;\n}\n\nstruct BorrowLendUserTokenState {\n    BasisAndValue borrow;\n    BasisAndValue supply;\n}\n\n```\nhttps://hyperevmscan.io/address/0x0d547f267d9efc4b6601b255507120daff34a581#code\n\n\n`bridgeYieldFromL1()` then trusts accountant.surplus() and does not reduce outstandingL1Principal, so ignored borrow debt can be converted into declared yield.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix/blob/3d94be1361ca01d959f9165a78f0d75c5657fe3e/src/core/MonetrixVault.sol#L247-L252\n\n\n# Attack Path\n\n1. Users deposit USDC and receive USDM.\n2. Principal is bridged to HyperCore and held in Portfolio Margin / supplied positions.\n3. The PM account borrows USDC against eligible collateral.\n4. accountant.totalBacking() counts supplied collateral but ignores the borrow liability.\n5. vault.yieldShortfall() treats the omitted borrow amount as surplus.\n6. The Operator bridges that false surplus as yield.\n7. settle() and distributeYield() route principal to the Foundation, Insurance Fund, and sUSDM as if it were real yield.\n\n# Impact\n\nUSDM can become undercollateralized while the protocol still reports full backing.\n\nThe ignored borrow debt is effectively socialized to USDM holders, while the false surplus is distributed as yield.",
  "proof_of_concept": "This PoC models the accounting root cause:\n\n* 1,000,000 USDC of USDM liabilities.\n* 1,000,000 USDC supplied in PM.\n* 100,000 USDC of supplied HYPE collateral.\n* 100,000 USDC of PM borrow debt.\n\nMonetrix reports a 100,000 USDC surplus and distributableSurplus() accepts it.\n\nIf the borrow debt is included, that surplus disappears.\n\nThe full attack path then uses the normal bridgeYieldFromL1() -> settle() -> distributeYield() flow described above to convert this false surplus into declared yield.\n\nAdd this PoC at `2026-04-monetrix/test`\n\nPortfolioMarginBorrowDebtPoC.t.sol\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\nimport {MonetrixAccountant} from \"../src/core/MonetrixAccountant.sol\";\nimport {PrecompileReader} from \"../src/core/PrecompileReader.sol\";\nimport {MonetrixAccessController} from \"../src/governance/MonetrixAccessController.sol\";\nimport {HyperCoreConstants} from \"../src/interfaces/HyperCoreConstants.sol\";\nimport {USDM} from \"../src/tokens/USDM.sol\";\nimport {MockUSDC} from \"./mocks/MockUSDC.sol\";\n\ncontract PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile {\n    mapping(bytes32 => bytes) public responses;\n\n    function setResponse(bytes calldata callData, bytes calldata response) external {\n        responses[keccak256(callData)] = response;\n    }\n\n    fallback(bytes calldata data) external payable returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes memory response = responses[keccak256(data)];\n        if (response.length == 0) return new bytes(128);\n        return response;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract PMBorrowDebtVaultStub {\n    USDM public immutable usdm;\n    MonetrixAccountant public accountant;\n\n    address public multisigVault;\n    address public redeemEscrow;\n\n    constructor(USDM _usdm) {\n        usdm = _usdm;\n    }\n\n    function setAccountant(MonetrixAccountant _accountant) external {\n        accountant = _accountant;\n    }\n\n    function mintLiability(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        usdm.mint(to, amount);\n    }\n\n    function registerSupply(uint64 spotToken, uint32 perpIndex) external {\n        accountant.notifyVaultSupply(spotToken, perpIndex);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract PortfolioMarginBorrowDebtPoC is Test {\n    address admin = address(0xAD);\n    address user = address(0xBEEF);\n\n    uint32 constant HYPE_PERP = 1;\n    uint32 constant HYPE_TOKEN = 150;\n\n    MockUSDC usdc;\n    USDM usdm;\n    MonetrixAccountant accountant;\n    PMBorrowDebtVaultStub vault;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        vm.startPrank(admin);\n\n        MonetrixAccessController acl = MonetrixAccessController(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new MonetrixAccessController()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(MonetrixAccessController.initialize, (admin))\n                )\n            )\n        );\n        acl.grantRole(acl.GOVERNOR(), admin);\n\n        usdc = new MockUSDC();\n        usdm = USDM(address(new ERC1967Proxy(address(new USDM()), abi.encodeCall(USDM.initialize, (address(acl))))));\n        vault = new PMBorrowDebtVaultStub(usdm);\n        usdm.setVault(address(vault));\n\n        accountant = MonetrixAccountant(\n            address(\n                new ERC1967Proxy(\n                    address(new MonetrixAccountant()),\n                    abi.encodeCall(\n                        MonetrixAccountant.initialize,\n                        (address(vault), address(usdc), address(usdm), address(acl))\n                    )\n                )\n            )\n        );\n        vault.setAccountant(accountant);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        _installPrecompiles();\n        _mockPerpAccountValueZero();\n        _mockHypeMetadata();\n        _mockHypeOracleAtTenDollars();\n    }\n\n    function test_portfolioMarginBorrowDebtCreatesFalseDistributableSurplus() public {\n        uint256 liabilities = 1_000_000e6;\n        uint256 borrowDebt = 100_000e6;\n        uint256 suppliedHypeValue = 100_000e6;\n\n        vault.mintLiability(user, liabilities);\n        vault.registerSupply(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), 0);\n        vault.registerSupply(uint64(HYPE_TOKEN), HYPE_PERP);\n\n        _mockBorrowLend(\n            uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX),\n            uint64(borrowDebt * 100),\n            uint64(liabilities * 100)\n        );\n        _mockBorrowLend(uint64(HYPE_TOKEN), 0, uint64(10_000 * 1e8));\n\n        assertEq(accountant.totalBacking(), liabilities + suppliedHypeValue, \"borrow debt is not subtracted\");\n        assertEq(accountant.surplus(), int256(borrowDebt), \"borrow debt appears as surplus\");\n        assertEq(accountant.distributableSurplus(), int256(borrowDebt), \"false surplus passes yield gate\");\n        assertEq(accountant.totalBacking() - borrowDebt, liabilities, \"subtracting borrow removes all surplus\");\n    }\n\n    function _installPrecompiles() internal {\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_ACCOUNT_MARGIN_SUMMARY, address(new PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SPOT_BALANCE, address(new PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_ORACLE_PX, address(new PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_VAULT_EQUITY, address(new PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE, address(new PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_TOKEN_INFO, address(new PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile()).code);\n        vm.etch(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_PERP_ASSET_INFO, address(new PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile()).code);\n    }\n\n    function _mockPerpAccountValueZero() internal {\n        PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_ACCOUNT_MARGIN_SUMMARY)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(uint32(0), address(vault)),\n            abi.encode(int64(0), uint64(0), uint64(0), int64(0))\n        );\n    }\n\n    function _mockBorrowLend(uint64 token, uint64 borrowValue, uint64 supplyValue) internal {\n        PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(address(vault), token),\n            abi.encode(borrowValue, borrowValue, supplyValue, supplyValue)\n        );\n    }\n\n    function _mockHypeOracleAtTenDollars() internal {\n        PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_ORACLE_PX)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(HYPE_PERP),\n            abi.encode(uint64(100_000))\n        );\n    }\n\n    function _mockHypeMetadata() internal {\n        uint64[] memory spots = new uint64[](0);\n        PrecompileReader.TokenInfo memory tokenInfo = PrecompileReader.TokenInfo({\n            name: \"HYPE\",\n            spots: spots,\n            deployerTradingFeeShare: 0,\n            deployer: address(0),\n            evmContract: address(0),\n            szDecimals: 2,\n            weiDecimals: 8,\n            evmExtraWeiDecimals: 0\n        });\n        PrecompileReader.PerpAssetInfo memory perpInfo = PrecompileReader.PerpAssetInfo({\n            coin: \"HYPE\",\n            marginTableId: 0,\n            szDecimals: 2,\n            maxLeverage: 10,\n            onlyIsolated: false\n        });\n        PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_TOKEN_INFO)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(HYPE_TOKEN),\n            abi.encode(tokenInfo)\n        );\n        PMBorrowDebtMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_PERP_ASSET_INFO)).setResponse(\n            abi.encode(HYPE_PERP),\n            abi.encode(perpInfo)\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-path test/PortfolioMarginBorrowDebtPoC.t.sol -q\n```",
